## Time  & Space Complexity

Time Complexity:
- The algorithm iterates through the array once, which is O(n).
- Each element is pushed onto the stack once and popped at most once, leading to O(n) operations related to stack operations.
- Therefore, the overall time complexity is O(n).

Space Complexity:
- The auxiliary space includes the result array, which is O(n).
- The stack can hold at most all elements in the worst case, which is also O(n).
- Hence, the total space complexity is O(n).

In summary, both time and space complexities are linear, O(n).

